        <div
          style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 6px; padding: 2px 0px; font-size: 12px;"
        >
          <div
            style="display: flex; gap: 12px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;"
          >
            <label
              style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px;"
            >
              <span
                style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-weight: 600;"
              >
                Book-page gap
              </span>
              <input
                max="3600"
                min="0"
                step="10"
                style="width: 70px; padding: 4px 8px; text-align: center; border-radius: 6px; border: 1px solid rgb(58, 60, 86); background: rgb(34, 36, 56); color: rgb(214, 212, 224); font-size: 12px; outline: none;"
                type="number"
                value="120"
              />
              <span
                style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160);"
              >
                s
              </span>
            </label>
            <span
              style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-size: 11px; font-style: italic;"
            >
              Book pages wait this long after the last one, on top of the Rate: Goodreads blocks a run of book pages from one address.
            </span>
          </div>
          <label
            style="display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 8px; cursor: pointer;"
          >
            <input
              style="margin-top: 2px;"
              type="checkbox"
            />
            <span
              style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 2px;"
            >
              <span
                style="color: rgb(214, 212, 224); font-weight: 600;"
              >
                Include non-fiction from Goodreads
              </span>
              <span
                style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-size: 11px;"
              >
                Off: books Goodreads files under Nonfiction, Self Help, Sports, Puzzles, Cookbooks, Reference or Picture Books aren't added to discovery. Turn on if you collect non-fiction.
              </span>
            </span>
          </label>
        </div>
        <div
          style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; padding: 10px 4px 14px 60px; border-bottom: 1px solid rgb(46, 48, 72); font-size: 12px;"
        >
          <div
            style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap;"
          >
            <span
              style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-weight: 600;"
            >
              Session state
            </span>
            <span
              style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 99px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; background: rgba(76, 184, 136, 0.133); color: rgb(76, 184, 136);"
            >
              Active
            </span>
            <span
              style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-size: 11px;"
            >
              last HTTP 200
            </span>
          </div>
          <div
            style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: 4px 12px; background: rgb(30, 32, 52); border: 1px solid rgb(46, 48, 72); border-radius: 6px; padding: 6px 10px;"
          >
            <div
              style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px;"
            >
              <span
                style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.4px;"
              >
                Book pages
              </span>
              <span
                style="color: rgb(76, 184, 136); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;"
              >
                OK
              </span>
            </div>
            <div
              style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px;"
            >
              <span
                style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.4px;"
              >
                List pages
              </span>
              <span
                style="color: rgb(76, 184, 136); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;"
              >
                OK
              </span>
            </div>
            <div
              style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 1px;"
            >
              <span
                style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-size: 10px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.4px;"
              >
                Autocomplete
              </span>
              <span
                style="color: rgb(76, 184, 136); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600;"
              >
                OK
              </span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div
            style="display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap;"
          >
            <button
              style="background: rgb(30, 32, 52); color: rgb(214, 212, 224); border: 1px solid rgb(58, 60, 86); border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; padding: 8px 14px; font-size: 14px;"
            >
              Run probe
            </button>
            <button
              style="background: rgb(30, 32, 52); color: rgb(214, 212, 224); border: 1px solid rgb(58, 60, 86); border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; cursor: pointer; padding: 8px 14px; font-size: 14px;"
            >
              Run burst (10×)
            </button>
          </div>
          <div
            style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-size: 11px; font-style: italic; line-height: 1.4;"
          >
            Goodreads sits behind AWS WAF bot protection, which turns away book pages far sooner than list pages. After a block, that kind of request backs off for 2 minutes, then 5, 10, 30 and 60 on repeated blocks, and clears on the next success; the others carry on. Run probe for a quick check (it goes out even while book pages back off); run burst to see how density holds. Mark as active ends every backoff now.
          </div>
        </div>
        <div
          style="padding: 10px 4px 12px 0px; font-size: 12px; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; border-top: 1px solid rgb(46, 48, 72); margin-top: 4px;"
        >
          <div
            style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; flex-wrap: wrap;"
          >
            <span
              style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-weight: 600;"
            >
              Goodreads cache worker
            </span>
            <span
              style="font-size: 11px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; padding: 3px 9px; border-radius: 99px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; background: rgba(224, 96, 96, 0.133); color: rgb(224, 96, 96);"
            >
              Cooldown
            </span>
            <span
              style="color: rgb(136, 134, 160); font-size: 11px;"
            >
              clears in 30m
            </span>
            <span
              style="flex: 1 1 0%;"
            />
            <div
              style="display: flex; gap: 0px; align-items: stretch;"
            >
              <button
                disabled=""
                style="padding: 4px 10px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; background: rgba(228, 184, 104, 0.133); color: rgb(228, 184, 104); border: 1px solid rgb(228, 184, 104); border-top-left-radius: 4px; border-bottom-left-radius: 4px; border-top-right-radius: 0px; border-bottom-right-radius: 0px; cursor: default; opacity: 1;"
                title="Worker fires every 30–90s round the clock."
              >
                Continuous
              </button>
              <button
                style="padding: 4px 10px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; background: rgb(30, 32, 52); color: rgb(236, 234, 244); border-width: 1px 1px 1px 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgb(46, 48, 72); border-image: none; border-top-left-radius: 0px; border-bottom-left-radius: 0px; border-top-right-radius: 0px; border-bottom-right-radius: 0px; cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;"
                title="Worker only runs inside the active-hours window below."
              >
                Scheduled
              </button>
              <button
                style="padding: 4px 10px; font-size: 11px; font-weight: 600; background: rgb(30, 32, 52); color: rgb(236, 234, 244); border-width: 1px 1px 1px 0px; border-style: solid; border-color: rgb(46, 48, 72); border-image: none; border-top-left-radius: 0px; border-bottom-left-radius: 0px; border-top-right-radius: 4px; border-bottom-right-radius: 4px; cursor: pointer; opacity: 1;"
                title="Worker stays idle; cache reads still hit existing rows."
              >
